# PDF Contract, Deliverable Submission & Billing Receipt — Implementation Plan

## Overview

A full end-to-end offer lifecycle overhaul. Contract + receipt documents tied to a revised status flow with proper work delivery and review steps. All confirmed decisions are locked in below.

---

## Revised Offer Lifecycle

```
FREELANCER submits offer
  → status: PENDING
  → Contract PDF generated, freelancerSigned = true
  → 📄 Contract card: "Awaiting client signature"

CLIENT reviews → accepts
  → status: ACCEPTED  (posting stays active/closed for new offers)
  → clientSigned = true on contract
  → 📄 Contract card: "Fully executed ✓"
  → 📦 Deliverables upload panel unlocked for freelancer

FREELANCER uploads final files (zip/pdf/etc via Uploadcare)
  → files stored but hidden from client (deliverableVisible = false)
  → FREELANCER clicks "Mark as Delivered"
  → status: DELIVERED
  → deliverableVisible = true  ← client can now see files
  → 🔔 Client notified

CLIENT reviews deliverables
  → "Mark as Completed"  → status: COMPLETED → 🧾 Receipt generated
  → "Mark as Unsatisfactory" → status: UNSATISFACTORY (no receipt)

AUTO: When ALL accepted offers for a posting
      reach COMPLETED or UNSATISFACTORY
  → Posting status → COMPLETED (automated, no manual trigger)
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The current `PostingService.updateStatus()` manually cascades `COMPLETED` to all accepted offers. **This block is removed.** Posting completion is now **automatic**, driven by offers, not the other way around.

> [!NOTE]
> `UNSATISFACTORY` triggers a **partial settlement modal** before the status is confirmed (see Section 3 — Receipt for UNSATISFACTORY). No dispute/resolution flow beyond this for now.

> [!NOTE]
> **Resubmit (canReapply) is removed entirely.** A freelancer can delete a canceled offer and create a new one instead. The `canReapply` flag, its backend logic, and its UI button are all removed.

